WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.976
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:07.840
SPEAKER: To get
started with Pub/Sub,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.620
first make sure the Pub/Sub API
is enabled for your project.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.320
Then go to the Pub/Sub page
in the Google Cloud Platform

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.730
console.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.070
Click Create a Topic.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.850
Enter a unique name
for your topic--

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.030
for example, My Topic.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:22.790
That's it.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.013
You've just created a
Cloud Pub/Sub topic.

00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:27.430
To add a subscription
to the topic

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.500
you've just created,
use the Display

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.150
menu for the topic
you've just created

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.670
and click New Subscription.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.460
Type a name for the
subscription, MySub.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.290
This is case-sensitive,
so do make sure

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.200
you capitalize the M and the S.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.830
Leave the delivery type
as Pull, and click Create.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.110
To publish a message
to the topic,

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.730
in the Overflow menu for the
topic you've just created,

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.430
click Publish Message.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.830
Enter Hello World in
the message field.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.810
Click Publish.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.560
To receive the message
you just published,

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.290
your subscription needs to
perform a pull operation.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.380
One way to do this is through
the G Cloud command line tool.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.540
You can use the Google
Cloud SDK locally.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.790
But here, we'll use the
in-console cloud shell

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.670
to run the following G Cloud
command from the guide.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.620
The message you sent
appears in the data field

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.270
of the command output.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.140
Congratulations.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.080
You've just created a Cloud
Pub/Sub topic, subscription,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.670
and pull request to
that subscription.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:22.720
[MUSIC PLAYING]

